.TH AJAIL 1 "" "ajail" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ajail \- run AppImages in a bubblewrap sandbox
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ajail
\fIFILE.AppImage\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.br
.B ajail run
[\fB\-\-compat\-env\fR] \fINAME\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.br
.B ajail run\-file
[\fB\-\-once\fR] [\fB\-\-mount\fR] [\fB\-\-compat\-env\fR] \fIFILE\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.br
.B ajail install
\fIFILE.AppImage\fR [\fB\-\-trash\fR] [\fB\-\-mount\fR [\fB\-\-move\fR]]
.br
.B ajail uninstall
\fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-purge\fR] [\fB\-\-discard\-image\fR]
.br
.B ajail restore
\fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIFOLDER\fR]
.br
.B ajail export
[\fINAME\fR | \fB\-\-default\fR | \fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B ajail import
\fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B ajail list
.br
.B ajail stop
\fINAME\fR
.br
.B ajail name
\fIFILE.AppImage\fR
.br
.B ajail preview
[\fINAME\fR]
.br
.B ajail on
|
.B off
|
.B status
|
.B check
.br
.B ajail desktop
\fB\-\-install\-menu\fR | \fB\-\-remove\-menu\fR
.br
.B ajail help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run an AppImage with its own private home and its own permissions. Only
.I /usr
and a few files in
.I /etc
are visible, the environment is rebuilt, and your real home is hidden except for the folders you share.
Unpacking happens in a separate sandbox with no network and no home. A seccomp filter blocks
.BR bpf ,
.BR perf_event_open ,
.B kexec_load
and similar calls, and
.BR socket (2)
is limited to Unix, IPv4, IPv6 and netlink sockets. Notifications and portals go through
.BR xdg\-dbus\-proxy (1),
which allows only the calls the permissions name.
.PP
After
.BR "ajail on" ,
double\-clicking an AppImage offers Install or Run once. Terminal launches never prompt. Only type 2 AppImages
work, and ajail refuses to run as root. Files passed as arguments, or through Open With, are shared for that run
only. The app name is the file name without version and architecture:
.I Foo\-1.2.3\-x86_64.AppImage
becomes
.IR Foo .
.PP
Settings are edited with
.BR ajail\-gui ;
the files are described under
.BR PERMISSIONS .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ajail FILE.AppImage [args]
Open an AppImage. When started from the file manager it offers Install or Run once; otherwise it runs sandboxed.
Files in
.I args
are shared for that run.
.TP
.B ajail run [\-\-compat\-env] NAME [args]
Run an installed app.
.B \-\-compat\-env
passes a short list of graphics and toolkit variables from your session into the sandbox for this run (the
permission
.B compat_env=1
does it every time). It goes before NAME.
.TP
.B ajail run\-file [\-\-once] [\-\-mount] [\-\-compat\-env] FILE
Run an AppImage without offering to install it.
.B \-\-once
deletes its unpacked copy on exit and never mounts.
.B \-\-mount
mounts the file instead of unpacking it (experimental).
.TP
.B ajail install FILE.AppImage [\-\-trash] [\-\-mount [\-\-move]]
Unpack it and add it to the app menu (name, icon, file types). The file is left where it is.
.B \-\-trash
moves it to the Trash.
.B \-\-mount
keeps it compressed and mounts it at launch (experimental; needs squashfuse, fuse3 and /dev/fuse); the image is
read by squashfuse outside the sandbox, so use it only for apps you trust.
.B \-\-move
(only with
.BR \-\-mount )
moves the file into ajail's folder instead of copying it, and falls back to a copy on a removable or network drive.
.TP
.B ajail uninstall NAME [\-\-purge] [\-\-discard\-image]
Remove the app from the app menu.
.B \-\-purge
also moves its data to the Trash. An AppImage that was moved into ajail is not deleted unless you pass
.BR \-\-discard\-image ;
use
.B restore
to get it back.
.TP
.B ajail restore NAME [\-\-keep] [\-\-to FOLDER]
Undo a compressed install that moved the file: put it back and uninstall.
.B \-\-keep
puts a copy back and leaves the app installed.
.B \-\-to
picks the folder.
.TP
.B ajail export [NAME | \-\-default | \-\-all] [\-o FILE] [\-\-force]
Write settings as one text file: the default permissions and every app's own (\fB\-\-all\fR, the default), the default
permissions only, or one app. Without
.B \-o
it prints to the terminal. The file is created readable by you only, and an existing file is replaced only with
.BR \-\-force .
Each settings file is a section starting with a line like
.BR "# [apps/NAME.conf]" ,
so the whole export is still a valid comment-and-settings text. The choices
.B ajail\-gui
remembers (open mode, install and disk\-space options, from ui.conf) are a section
.BR "# [ui.conf]" :
all of them for
.BR \-\-all ,
the global ones for
.BR \-\-default ,
and the app's own
.BI mount. NAME
and
.BI open_mode. NAME
for one app. Private homes, installed apps, the binfmt rule and the app menu entry are not included.
.TP
.B ajail import FILE [\-\-force]
Load an export made by
.BR "ajail export" ,
or \fB\-\fR for standard input. Settings files that do not exist yet are created. If a file exists and differs, nothing is
written unless
.B \-\-force
is given, which replaces those files. The ui.conf section is merged into your ui.conf: only the choices it names
change, and it counts as differing only when one of them is already set to another value. Imported values are checked
when an app starts, like hand-edited files.
.TP
.B ajail list
Show your apps and which are running.
.TP
.B ajail stop NAME
Stop a running app.
.TP
.B ajail name FILE.AppImage
Show the name ajail uses for this file.
.TP
.B ajail preview [NAME]
Print the bwrap command that would run.
.TP
.B ajail on | off | status | check
.B on
sends every AppImage through ajail (it registers a binfmt_misc rule and asks for your password);
.B off
removes the rule;
.B status
shows which it is;
.B check
lists what is missing on this machine, with the install command for your distribution.
.TP
.B ajail help
Print the list of commands.
.TP
.B ajail desktop \-\-install\-menu
Add ajail\-gui to your app menu.
.B \-\-remove\-menu
takes it out again. It needs ajail\-gui installed as a root\-owned file in
.IR /usr/local/bin :
only such a copy is ever started from the menu, so a program running as you cannot replace it.
.SH PERMISSIONS
Plain
.I key=value
files: the defaults for every app, and one file per app that overrides them. List entries add up, except
.BR xdg .
Spaces around
.B =
are fine and
.B #
starts a comment. A line ajail cannot use (unknown key, a value the key does not take, no
.BR = )
is skipped with a warning in the terminal and in the log, never silently.
.PP
Switches (0 or 1, default in brackets):
.BR net " (1),"
.BR net_private " (0, needs pasta),"
.BR sound " (1, includes the microphone),"
.BR gpu " (1),"
.BR gpu_render_only " (0),"
.BR wayland " (1, a restricted socket where the desktop supports Wayland security contexts),"
.BR wayland_strict " (automatic: on where the desktop supports Wayland security contexts, otherwise off; 1 gives the app no Wayland unless its socket can be restricted),"
.BR x11 " (0, weaker isolation),"
.BR portals " (1),"
.BR portal_screenshot " (1),"
.BR portal_screencast " (1),"
.BR portal_notification " (1),"
.BR portal_openuri " (1),"
.BR portal_print " (1),"
.BR portal_trash " (1),"
.BR portal_email " (1),"
.BR portal_inhibit " (1),"
.BR portal_network " (1),"
.BR tray " (0),"
.BR a11y " (0, a screen reader such as Orca can read the app through a filtered copy of the accessibility bus, made with xdg\-dbus\-proxy and the rules Flatpak uses: the app can publish its widgets and ask who is listening, but cannot read other apps or send keys and clicks; QT_LINUX_ACCESSIBILITY_ALWAYS_ON=1 and GNOME_ACCESSIBILITY=1 are set so Qt and Firefox switch their accessibility support on; works without portals),"
.BR gnome_shell " (0, the browser's GNOME Shell connector can call ListExtensions, GetExtensionInfo, GetExtensionErrors and InstallRemoteExtension on org.gnome.Shell.Extensions at /org/gnome/Shell, read the Shell's properties and hear its extension signals, and own org.gnome.BrowserConnector; the Shell asks before it installs anything and Eval stays closed; works without portals),"
.BR gnome_shell_manage " (0, with gnome_shell also EnableExtension, DisableExtension and UninstallExtension),"
.BR kde " (0, the browser's Plasma integration can own org.kde.plasma.browser_integration and org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.plasma\-browser\-integration (each also with a \-PID suffix), show downloads through org.kde.JobViewServerV2.requestView and the job objects Plasma hands out, and call Inhibit and UnInhibit on org.freedesktop.PowerManagement.Inhibit; nothing is talk, and KDE Connect stays closed; works without portals),"
.BR bluetooth " (0, the app can use org.bluez on the system bus, through xdg\-dbus\-proxy, for example Web Bluetooth; it reaches nearby devices even with net=0),"
.BR battery " (0, the app can use org.freedesktop.UPower on the system bus, through xdg\-dbus\-proxy, to read the battery level and power state),"
.BR avahi " (0, the app can use org.freedesktop.Avahi on the system bus, through xdg\-dbus\-proxy, to find services on your local network by name, such as printers and Cast devices),"
.BR camera " (0),"
.BR input " (0),"
.BR compat_env " (0),"
.BR ssh_agent " (0),"
.BR printing " (0),"
.BR theme " (1),"
.BR app_writable " (0, for apps that fail with Read\-only file system under /app: what they write goes to a separate layer and the app's own files stay unchanged; needs bubblewrap 0.11+),"
.BR userns " (0; 1 lets Electron and Chromium apps make their own sandbox; 0 needs bubblewrap 0.8+),"
.BR tmp_home " (0, private home erased on exit),"
.BR privacy " (0, minimal /etc/passwd, /etc/group and /etc/hosts, the hostname ajail and no Account portal),"
.BR single_instance " (0, one private folder per app from $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is bound into every sandbox of it and TMPDIR points there, so a second launch can find the first, as Chrome does with its singleton socket; /tmp stays private)"
and
.BR harden " (0, also blocks io_uring_*, userfaultfd, process_vm_*, kcmp, pidfd_getfd and the new mount calls (open_tree, move_mount, fsopen, fsconfig, fsmount, fspick, mount_setattr); may break apps)."
.PP
.B gtk_portal
is auto (the default), 1 or 0. With
.B portals=1
it decides whether GTK programs are told to use the file chooser portal (GTK_USE_PORTAL=1). auto sets it, except when the cursor size
in your desktop settings is 0, which crashes GTK; ajail then leaves it unset and logs one line saying why. 1 and 0 set it or leave it
unset for that app whatever the cursor size. Qt programs are not affected.
.PP
Limits (0 means none; need
.BR "systemd\-run \-\-user" ):
.B mem_max
(MB),
.B cpu_max
(percent of one core) and
.BR tasks_max .
.PP
List keys:
.B allow=PATH
(read and write),
.B allow_ro=PATH
(read only),
.B xdg=NAME[:ro|:none]
(download, documents, pictures, music, videos or desktop),
.B env=VAR=value,
.B talk=NAME
(an extra D\-Bus name) and
.B portal=NAME
(turn on RemoteDesktop, InputCapture, DynamicLauncher or Background; needs
.BR portals=1 ;
.B portal=\-NAME
turns one off again, which is how to drop Location, GlobalShortcuts, Usb, Clipboard, FileTransfer, Wallpaper or Secret, the seven that are on by default). Shared paths must be non\-hidden items in your home or under
.IR /mnt ,
.I /media
or
.IR /run/media/$USER .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ajail/default.conf
Settings for every app.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ajail/apps/NAME.conf
Settings for one app; they override the default.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ajail/ui.conf
Choices made in ajail\-gui (open mode, install and disk\-space options).
The line
.BI mount. NAME =0|1
sets compressed installs for one app and beats the global choice.
.TP
.I ~/.appimage\-homes/NAME
The private home of NAME.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ajail/apps/NAME
An installed app.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ajail/ajail.log
The log of every run.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/io.github.outusuke.ajail.Gui.desktop
The app menu entry for ajail\-gui, made by
.BR "ajail desktop \-\-install\-menu" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The app's own status, or 128 plus the signal number if a signal ended it. ajail itself exits with 1 when it cannot
start the app (bad option, missing bubblewrap, no Wayland session, running as root).
.SH LIMITS
Only type 2 AppImages work. The private home is tied to the app's Name=, so a different app with the same file name
is refused instead of inheriting the first one's data. Several defaults (net, sound, gpu) favour apps that
work out of the box; for an app you do not trust set
.BR "harden=1 net=0 sound=0" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bwrap (1),
.BR xdg\-dbus\-proxy (1),
.BR systemd\-run (1)
